mission "A Debt in the Admiralty"
    name "A Debt in the Admiralty"
    description "Carry proof of the lost expedition's secret orders to a naval officer who can authenticate them."
    source "Mermaid's Rest"
    destination "Havana"
    reward 1395
    speaker offer "Commodore Wycliffe"
    speaker visit "Commodore Wycliffe"
    speaker complete "Commodore Wycliffe"
    to offer
        has "The Black Tide Ambush: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `A bundle of sealed orders lies on Wycliffe's desk. The wax is old, but the signatures appear to have survived the years.`
            `Commodore Wycliffe turns one of the papers toward the light. "We need a naval officer to authenticate these orders. I can tell you the seals look genuine, but I cannot ask a court to accept my word alone."`
            choice
                `"I will put my ship to it. Let us get underway."`
                    accept
                `"Why ask a captain instead of going to the authorities?"`
                    goto details
                `"I would rather not have my name in these papers."`
                    close
            label details
                `He places the documents in a leather case. "Take the proof to someone who can compare the signatures with the admiralty register. If they match, we will know who sent the expedition west—and who knew about it."`
                choice
                    `"Agreed. Let us make certain the truth reaches daylight."`
                        accept
                    `"I have decided. I will not be sailing."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted A Debt in the Admiralty. Carry proof of the lost expedition's secret orders to a naval officer who can authenticate them."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At Havana, Wycliffe places the documents before the naval officer. The seals and signatures match the old register. "That makes the orders real," he says. "It does not make them lawful, but it gives us a name to question."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Wycliffe secures the papers again. "The admiralty cannot dismiss these as tavern gossip now. Keep the original safe. A document like this can start a trial—or a war—depending on whose hands it reaches."`
        log "Completed A Debt in the Admiralty. Received 1395 gold. Carry proof of the lost expedition's secret orders to a naval officer who can authenticate them."
